rties: introductory quantum chemistry, basic organic chemistry, non-covalent interactions, electrochemistry and surfaces and interfaces. Materials addressed include polymers, biopolymers, ceramics and glasses, optical materials and metallic, semiconductor and silica nanoparticles.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: CHEM 2090, MATH 2930,\u00a0PHYS 2214.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 353883, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "MSE", "catalogNbr": "3030", "titleShort": "Thermo of Cond Systems", "titleLong": "Thermodynamics of Condensed Systems", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1313, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:00AM", "timeEnd": "12:30PM", "startDt": "05/24/2018", "endDt": "07/04/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "mot1", "firstName": "Mike", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Thompson"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 4, "netid": "jct39", "firstName": "Julie", "middleName": "C.", "lastName": "Wright"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Thurston Hall 205", "bldgDescr": "Thurston Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "THR205", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1777"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/24/2018", "endDt": "07/04/2018", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Introduces the three laws of thermodynamics as the fundamental basis for thermal and chemical equilibrium, coupled with statistical mechanical interpretations for entropy.\u00a0 Applies these principles to understand the equilibrium behavior of matter, with a focus on condensed liquid and solid phases.\u00a0 Develops concepts of phase equilibria, phase diagrams, chemical reactions, solution behavior and electrochemistry.\u00a0 Includes an introduction to statistical mechanics and applications in ideal gas behavior, gas and crystal heat capacity, and electron Fermi-Dirac statistics.\u00a0 Applications and examples will be drawn from a range of sub-disciplines spanning metallurgy to polymers.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite:\u00a0PHYS 1112\u00a0. Corequisite: PHYS 2214\u00a0and\u00a0 MSE 2610\u00a0or equivalent background.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 353888, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "MSE", "catalogNbr": "3110", "titleShort": "Junior Laboratory I", "titleLong": "Junior Laboratory I", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LAB", "ssrComponentLong": "Laboratory", "section": "401", "classNbr": 1314, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:30PM", "timeEnd": "04:30PM", "startDt": "05/24/2018", "endDt": "07/04/2018", "instructors": [], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Bard Hall 258", "bldgDescr": "Bard Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "BRD258", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=2765"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/24/2018", "endDt": "07/04/2018", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 2, "unitsMaximum": 2, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LAB"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Practical laboratory covering the characterization of materials, analysis of data, and presentation of results. Labs are based on concepts from the chemistry of materials (MSE 3010) and thermodynamics of condensed systems (MSE 3030) courses. Experiments include calorimetry, spectroscopic characterization, nanoparticle growth, polymer OLED devices, and molecular origins of spectral data features. Comprehensive data analysis including statistical data analysis, curve fitting and experimental uncertainty is emphasized. Includes an introduction to formal technical writing.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: ENGRD 2610/MSE 2610\u00a0or ENGRD 2620/MSE 2620. Corequisite: MSE 3010, MSE 3030\u00a0or permission of instructor.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 368535, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "MSE", "catalogNbr": "3111", "titleShort": "Tech. & Prof. Skills", "titleLong": "Technical and Professional Skills", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1317, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:30PM", "timeEnd": "03:45PM", "startDt": "05/24/2018", "endDt": "07/04/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "lrt5", "firstName": "Lisa", "middleName": "Rose", "lastName": "Thompson"}], "pattern": "W", "facilityDescr": "Bard Hall 258", "bldgDescr": "Bard Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "BRD258", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3150"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Ma